---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../utils/paths';

const composeCode = `curl -fsSL https://krabka.io/quickstart/docker-compose.yml -o docker-compose.yml
docker compose up -d`;

const composeReadyCode = `KAFKA_TOOLS=docker.io/apache/kafka@sha256:01b9a4030e54c6068e66eb3ba4cb82c0d89238629ef1c30d79b86036bf89b1b7
docker run --rm --network "container:$(docker compose ps -q broker)" "$KAFKA_TOOLS" \\
  /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --list`;

const composeVerifyCode = `KAFKA_TOOLS=docker.io/apache/kafka@sha256:01b9a4030e54c6068e66eb3ba4cb82c0d89238629ef1c30d79b86036bf89b1b7
KAFKA_NETWORK="container:$(docker compose ps -q broker)"
docker run --rm --network "$KAFKA_NETWORK" "$KAFKA_TOOLS" /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-topics.sh \\
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --create --if-not-exists --topic quickstart-events --partitions 1 --replication-factor 1
printf 'hello krabka\\n' | docker run --rm -i --network "$KAFKA_NETWORK" "$KAFKA_TOOLS" \\
  /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-producer.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic quickstart-events
docker run --rm --network "$KAFKA_NETWORK" "$KAFKA_TOOLS" /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh \\
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic quickstart-events --from-beginning --max-messages 1 --timeout-ms 30000`;

const composeCleanupCode = `docker compose down --volumes`;

const helmCode = `kubectl apply -f https://krabka.io/quickstart/crds.yaml
helm repo add krabka https://krabka.io/charts
helm repo update
helm install krabka-operator krabka/krabka-operator --version 0.5.0 --skip-crds \\
  --namespace krabka-system --create-namespace \\
  --set image.repository=ghcr.io/krabka-io/krabka-operator \\
  --set-string image.digest=sha256:413e3231a735c2d73fbdf665d61d0cae026540beff3a4f53c184983a19d5c645
kubectl rollout status deployment/krabka-operator-krabka-operator -n krabka-system --timeout=5m
kubectl apply -f https://krabka.io/quickstart/krabka-cluster.yaml
kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready kafka/m20-quickstart --timeout=10m
kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready kafkatopic/quickstart --timeout=5m`;

const helmVerifyCode = `KAFKA_TOOLS=docker.io/apache/kafka@sha256:01b9a4030e54c6068e66eb3ba4cb82c0d89238629ef1c30d79b86036bf89b1b7
kubectl run kafka-tools --image="$KAFKA_TOOLS" --restart=Never --rm -i --command -- \\
  /bin/bash -lc "printf 'hello krabka\\n' | /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-producer.sh --bootstrap-server m20-quickstart-broker-headless.default.svc.cluster.local:9092 --topic quickstart && /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --bootstrap-server m20-quickstart-broker-headless.default.svc.cluster.local:9092 --topic quickstart --from-beginning --max-messages 1 --timeout-ms 30000"`;

const helmCleanupCode = `kubectl delete kafkatopic/quickstart
kubectl delete kafka/m20-quickstart
kubectl delete kafkanodepool/brokers --ignore-not-found
helm uninstall krabka-operator -n krabka-system
kubectl delete -f https://krabka.io/quickstart/crds.yaml`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quickstart Guide"
  description="Start a local krabka broker, check readiness, create a topic, and produce and read a record with containerized Kafka tools. Includes Kubernetes and separate cleanup."
  currentSlug="/docs/quickstart"
>
  <div class="space-y-6 font-sans text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">Run krabka and read your first record</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-400">Use the Kafka tools in a container to complete one round trip. The broker stays running for your next task.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Before you start</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li>Install Docker with Docker Compose, and start Docker.</li>
      <li>Use a Bash terminal with <code>curl</code>. On Windows, use a Bash terminal connected to Docker.</li>
      <li>Use an empty working directory and keep port <code>9092</code> free. Run each local step in that directory.</li>
      <li>The supplied broker image uses <code>linux/amd64</code>. Review the <a href={getPath('/docs/operations')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">operations guides</a> before deploying your own cluster.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To try without installing software, open the <a href={getPath('/docs/browser-tools')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">browser tools</a>. Cluster Lab runs real brokers in your browser; its phone mode is for viewing.</p>

    <h2 id="local" class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">1. Start a local broker</h2>
    <p>Download the Compose file and start its single-node KRaft broker.</p>
    <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3">
      <div class="flex justify-between gap-3 items-center"><span>Start</span><button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 hover:bg-white/10" data-copy={composeCode} aria-label="Copy local startup commands">Copy</button></div>
      <CodeBlock code={composeCode} lang="bash" />
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">2. Check that the broker is ready</h2>
    <p>The Kafka tools use the broker container's network. Continue when the topic-list command completes without an error; the list can be empty before you create a topic. If startup is still in progress, repeat this check. Use <code>docker compose logs broker</code> to inspect a failed startup.</p>
    <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3">
      <div class="flex justify-between gap-3 items-center"><span>Check readiness</span><button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 hover:bg-white/10" data-copy={composeReadyCode} aria-label="Copy local readiness check">Copy</button></div>
      <CodeBlock code={composeReadyCode} lang="bash" />
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">3. Create a topic, produce, and consume</h2>
    <p>Create <code>quickstart-events</code>, send <code>hello krabka</code>, and read one record. You can repeat these commands with the same topic.</p>
    <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3">
      <div class="flex justify-between gap-3 items-center"><span>Verify the round trip</span><button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 hover:bg-white/10" data-copy={composeVerifyCode} aria-label="Copy local record round trip">Copy</button></div>
      <CodeBlock code={composeVerifyCode} lang="bash" />
    </div>
    <p>The consumer prints <code>hello krabka</code> and exits after one record. If it times out, confirm that readiness passes and that the producer finished successfully.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Choose your next task</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <a href={getPath('/get-started#clients')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50"><h3 class="font-bold text-white">Connect your application →</h3><p class="mt-1 text-gray-400">Use a client example, including a downloadable JavaScript project.</p></a>
      <a href={getPath('/docs/operations')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50"><h3 class="font-bold text-white">Operate a cluster →</h3><p class="mt-1 text-gray-400">Find recovery and upgrade procedures with their version scope.</p></a>
    </div>

    <details class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 p-5 space-y-3">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-white">Optional: clean up the local broker</summary>
      <p>This stops the local cluster and deletes its Docker volume, including all records. Keep the cluster running to try a client example.</p>
      <button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 hover:bg-white/10" data-copy={composeCleanupCode} aria-label="Copy local cleanup commands">Copy cleanup</button>
      <CodeBlock code={composeCleanupCode} lang="bash" />
    </details>

    <h2 id="kubernetes" class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Kubernetes option</h2>
    <p>Use a disposable Kubernetes cluster with <code>kubectl</code> and Helm configured. These commands use the default namespace for a three-node broker cluster and <code>krabka-system</code> for the operator. Use a cluster without another installation of these CRDs.</p>
    <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3">
      <div class="flex justify-between gap-3 items-center"><span>Start and wait for readiness</span><button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 hover:bg-white/10" data-copy={helmCode} aria-label="Copy Kubernetes startup commands">Copy</button></div>
      <CodeBlock code={helmCode} lang="bash" />
    </div>
    <p>Continue when both waits report their Ready condition. The manifest creates <code>quickstart</code>. Run Kafka tools inside the cluster because brokers advertise in-cluster names.</p>
    <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3">
      <div class="flex justify-between gap-3 items-center"><span>Verify the Kubernetes round trip</span><button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 hover:bg-white/10" data-copy={helmVerifyCode} aria-label="Copy Kubernetes record round trip">Copy</button></div>
      <CodeBlock code={helmVerifyCode} lang="bash" />
    </div>
    <p>The consumer prints <code>hello krabka</code>. See <a href={getPath('/docs/operator')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">operator configuration</a> to change this deployment.</p>
    <details class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 p-5 space-y-3">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-white">Optional: clean up the Kubernetes example</summary>
      <p>These commands remove the example cluster, topic, operator, and krabka CRDs. Deleting CRDs affects every resource of those types; run this only in the disposable cluster used for this example. Check your storage policy before removing persistent volumes.</p>
      <button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 hover:bg-white/10" data-copy={helmCleanupCode} aria-label="Copy Kubernetes cleanup commands">Copy cleanup</button>
      <CodeBlock code={helmCleanupCode} lang="bash" />
    </details>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
